    skos:definition "Compounds derived from oxoacids $\\ce{R_{k}E(=O)_{l}(OH)_{m}}\\ (l \\neq 0)$ by replacing an $\\ce{OH}$ group by the NHPh group or derivative formed by ring substitution; N-phenyl amides, e.g. $\\ce{CH3C(=O)NHPh}$ acetanilide.See: amidesSalts formed by replacement of a nitrogen-bound hydron of aniline by a metal or other cation, e.g. $\\ce{NaNHPh}$ sodium anilide."@en ;
